From: VeCI field triage (based on openwrt/mt76 PR #1166)
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7603: defer watchdog on channel error

MT7628 channel-error recovery must not synchronously invoke mac_work
while mt76_set_channel() holds dev->mutex. Queue it after the current
callback returns. Upstream original: https://github.com/openwrt/mt76/pull/1166

DO NOT install as an unverified runtime module. Apply to exact firmware
source tree, compile with matching kernel/SDK and validate vermagic,
loaded module ABI, and isolated-device regression tests.

--- a/mt7603/main.c
+++ b/mt7603/main.c
@@ -193,7 +193,8 @@ int mt7603_set_channel(struct mt76_phy *mphy)
 	tasklet_enable(&dev->mt76.pre_tbtt_tasklet);
 
 	if (failed)
-		mt7603_mac_work(&dev->mphy.mac_work.work);
+		ieee80211_queue_delayed_work(mt76_hw(dev),
+					     &dev->mphy.mac_work, 0);
 
 	return ret;
 }
